      <h2>Conclusion</h2>
      <p>Stop asking "which OS is best" and start asking "which OS fits my use case." All three are excellent in 2026 — and the gap between them is narrower than forum arguments suggest.</p>
      <p>Pick <strong>Ubuntu 24.04 LTS</strong> for learning, Docker, AI inference, GPU workloads, and general-purpose use. Pick <strong>AlmaLinux 9</strong> for cPanel / Plesk hosting businesses and any workload that values the RHEL ABI plus commercial backing. Pick <strong>Rocky Linux 9</strong> for the same RHEL compatibility with a community-first governance model.</p>
      <p>Whatever you pick, do not run CentOS 7. There are no more security patches, and every month of delay is a month your server is exposed. The <code>elevate</code> and <code>migrate2rocky</code> tools make the migration painless — most 4GB RackNerd VPS instances finish in under 30 minutes.</p>

